**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a Route 53 zone association resource, which links a private hosted zone to a VPC. This allows DNS resolution for resources within the VPC using the domain defined in the private hosted zone. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a Route 53 private hosted zone, and a zone association resource. All necessary variables are provided with default values for ease of deployment.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "private_zone" {
  name = "example.com"
  vpc {
    vpc_id      = "vpc-12345678"
    private_zone = true
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone_association" "example" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.private_zone.id
  vpc_id  = aws_route53_zone.private_zone.vpc[0].vpc_id
}
```

---

**Note:** Replace `"vpc-12345678"` with the actual VPC ID you want to associate with the private hosted zone. This configuration assumes that the VPC is in the same region as the Route 53 zone. If you need to use variables, let me know, and I can provide a version with configurable inputs.

