This Terraform configuration creates an Elastic Beanstalk worker environment designed to run batch processing jobs. It includes the following components:

- An IAM role (`eb_ec2_role`) and instance profile (`eb_ec2_profile`) for the Elastic Beanstalk EC2 instances.
- An Elastic Beanstalk application (`batch_job_app`) and an application version (`version`) for deploying the worker environment.
- An S3 bucket (`sampleapril26426`) and an object (`examplebucket_object`) for storing application code or logs.
- An SQS queue (`batch_job_queue`) for handling batch job messages.

The configuration ensures that all necessary resources are created and properly linked, with default values provided for any variables used.

