**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration defines a variable `cluster_name` of type string. It creates an AWS EKS cluster with the name derived from the `cluster_name` variable. The EKS cluster is associated with an IAM role that has the necessary permissions to manage the EKS cluster and its resources. The configuration includes the setup of a VPC with subnets for networking, defines an IAM role with appropriate policies, and uses `local-exec` provisioners to manage the `kubectl` configuration during the creation and destruction of the EKS cluster. All required resources and variables are fully specified and ready for deployment.

---

**Terraform HCL Code:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  type        = string
  description = "Name of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "my-eks-cluster"
}

# VPC and Subnets (example setup, adjust as needed)
resource "aws_vpc" "eks_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "eks-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "eks_subnet1" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.eks_vpc.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
  tags = {
    Name = "eks-subnet1"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "eks_subnet2" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.eks_vpc.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.2.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2b"
  tags = {
    Name = "eks-subnet2"
  }
}

# IAM Role for EKS Cluster
resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_role" {
  name = "eks-role-${var.cluster_name}"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "eks.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_role_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSReadOnlyAccess"
}

# EKS Cluster
resource "aws_eks_cluster" "eks_cluster" {
  name     = var.cluster_name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_role.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = [
      aws_subnet.eks_subnet1.id,
      aws_subnet.eks_subnet2.id,
    ]
  }

  # Wait for the cluster to be ready before proceeding
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.eks_role_policy]

  # Provisioner to configure kubectl after cluster creation
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = "aws eks update-kubeconfig --name ${var.cluster_name} --region us-west-2"
  }

  # Provisioner to clean up kubectl config on destroy
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    when = destroy
    command = "aws eks delete-kubeconfig --name ${var.cluster_name} --region us-west-2"
  }
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- This configuration assumes a basic VPC setup with two subnets. You may need to adjust the VPC and subnet configuration based on your actual network layout.
- The `AmazonEKSReadOnlyAccess` policy is used for the IAM role. You can replace it with a more specific policy if needed.
- The `local-exec` provisioners are used to manage the `kubectl` configuration locally. Ensure that the AWS CLI is installed and configured on the machine running Terraform.
- The provider version and AWS provider version are compatible with Terraform 1.9.8 and `hashicorp/aws ~> 5.75`.

