**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS S3 bucket named `wellcomecollection-platform-infra` with the following features:

- **Preventive Destruction Measures:** A `terraform_destroy` block is used to prevent accidental deletion of the bucket.
- **Access Control:** The bucket's ACL is set to `private` to ensure only the bucket owner has full control.
- **Versioning:** Versioning is enabled to keep track of all changes to objects in the bucket.
- **Lifecycle Policies:**
  - Objects with the prefix `tmp/` are automatically deleted after 30 days.
  - Old versions of objects are transitioned to the `STANDARD_IA` storage class after 30 days.
  - Noncurrent versions of objects are deleted after 90 days.

The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, sets the region to `us-east-1`, and ensures all resources are fully declared and deployable with Terraform 1.9.8 and AWS provider 5.75.

---

**Terraform HCL Code:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "platform_infra" {
  bucket = "wellcomecollection-platform-infra"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration" "platform_infra_lifecycle" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.platform_infra.bucket

  rule {
    id      = "tmp_prefix_deletion"
    status  = "Enabled"
    prefix  = "tmp/"
    days    = 30
    expiration {
      days = 30
    }
  }

  rule {
    id      = "transition_old_versions"
    status  = "Enabled"
    prefix  = ""
    days    = 30
    transition {
      storage_class = "STANDARD_IA"
      days          = 30
    }
  }

  rule {
    id      = "delete_noncurrent_versions"
    status  = "Enabled"
    prefix  = ""
    days    = 90
    noncurrent_version_expiration {
      days = 90
    }
  }
}
```

