**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates two AWS S3 buckets with distinct names. One bucket is configured with a private ACL, while the other is set to allow log delivery writes. S3 bucket logging is enabled on the first bucket, and the logs are directed to the second bucket. A log file prefix is specified to organize the log files. The configuration ensures that all resources are properly linked and that dependencies are correctly defined.

---

**Terraform HCL Configuration:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define variables with defaults
variable "bucket_prefix" {
  default = "terraform-s3-bucket"
}

variable "log_prefix" {
  default = "s3-logs/"
}

# Create the first S3 bucket (private)
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "private_bucket" {
  bucket = "${var.bucket_prefix}-private"
  acl    = "private"
}

# Create the second S3 bucket (log delivery write access)
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "log_bucket" {
  bucket = "${var.bucket_prefix}-log"
  acl    = "log-delivery-write"
}

# Enable logging on the private bucket, sending logs to the log bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket_logging" "private_bucket_logging" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.private_bucket.id
  target_bucket = aws_s3_bucket.log_bucket.id
  target_prefix = var.log_prefix
}
```

---

This configuration is ready to be applied with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`. It ensures that the S3 buckets are created with the correct access control and logging settings, and that the logging is directed to the appropriate bucket with a specified prefix.

