This Terraform configuration creates a VPC with three subnets: one public subnet and two private subnets. It provisions an EC2 instance in the public subnet to act as a web server, an EC2 instance in one of the private subnets to act as an application server, and an RDS instance in the other private subnet to serve as a database. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a VPC with internet gateway, route tables, and security groups for each instance. IAM roles are created for the EC2 instances to allow them to communicate with RDS and other AWS services.

