**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration will create an IAM role with a policy that allows Redshift to access AWS services (such as S3 for data loading). It will then create a Redshift cluster and associate the IAM role with the cluster. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, default values for variables, and ensures that all resources are fully specified and deployable.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an IAM role for Redshift
resource "aws_iam_role" "redshift_role" {
  name = "redshift_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = {
        Service = "redshift.amazonaws.com"
      }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

# Attach a policy to the IAM role to allow Redshift to access S3
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "redshift_s3_access" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.redshift_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
}

# Create a Redshift cluster
