**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that is configured to deliver data to a specific DynamoDB table. The configuration includes the necessary IAM role and policy to allow the Kinesis Firehose to write data to the DynamoDB table. The Kinesis Firehose is set up as a streaming destination, and the configuration assumes that the source of the data (e.g., a Kinesis Data Stream or another source) is already defined elsewhere.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define a variable for the DynamoDB table name
variable "dynamodb_table_name" {
  description = "Name of the DynamoDB table to which the Kinesis Firehose will deliver data"
  default     = "example-dynamodb-table"
}

# Create an IAM role for Kinesis Firehose
resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_role" {
  name = "firehose_delivery_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

# Attach the necessary IAM policy to the role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "firehose_dynamodb" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonKinesisFirehoseForRedshiftAndDynamoDB"
}

# Create a Kinesis Firehose delivery stream
resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "dynamodb_stream" {
  name        = "firehose-to-dynamodb"
  destination = "dynamodb"

  dynamodb_destination_configuration {
    role_arn       = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn
    table_name     = var.dynamodb_table_name
    payload_format = "JSON"
  }

  # Optional: If you want to use a source like a Kinesis Data Stream, you can reference it here
  # kinesis_source_configuration {
  #   kinesis_stream_arn = aws_kinesis_stream.example.arn
  #   role_arn           = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn
  # }
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- This configuration assumes that the DynamoDB table already exists or will be created separately.
- If you want to use a Kinesis Data Stream as the source, you can uncomment and modify the `kinesis_source_configuration` block accordingly.
- The IAM policy used is a managed policy that allows Firehose to write to DynamoDB. You can customize it if needed for more granular control.

