**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a custom Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) parameter group. A DAX parameter group allows you to modify the default configuration parameters for a DAX cluster. This is useful for tuning performance, enabling features, or adjusting settings specific to your application's needs. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a DAX parameter group resource, and a variable for the parameter group name with a default value.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "dax_parameter_group_name" {
  description = "Name of the DAX parameter group"
  default     = "my-dax-parameter-group"
}

resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "example" {
  name         = var.dax_parameter_group_name
  description  = "Custom DAX parameter group for application tuning"
  parameters {
    "max-connections" = "1000"
    "query-cache-size" = "1024"
    "log-level" = "INFO"
  }
}
```

This configuration will create a DAX parameter group with the specified name and custom parameters. You can modify the parameters in the `parameters` block to suit your specific use case.

