**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an **Amazon ElastiCache** cluster using **Redis** to reduce the number of direct database calls. The ElastiCache cluster will act as an in-memory data store, caching frequently accessed data from the database. This setup improves application performance and reduces the load on the underlying database.

The configuration includes:
- An ElastiCache Redis cluster with a single node (for simplicity).
- A VPC and subnet for the ElastiCache cluster.
- A security group to allow traffic between the application and the ElastiCache cluster.
- A default provider configuration for AWS in the `us-east-1` region.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "main-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "main" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  tags = {
    Name = "main-subnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "elasti_cache_sg" {
  name        = "elasti-cache-sg"
  description = "Allow traffic to ElastiCache"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.main.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 6379
    to_port     = 6379
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "elasti-cache-sg"
  }
}

resource "aws_elasticache_cluster" "redis_cache" {
  cluster_id           = "my-redis-cache"
  engine               = "redis"
  engine_version       = "6.x"
  node_type            = "cache.t2.micro"
  num_cache_nodes      = 1
  parameter_group_name = "default.redis6.x"
  subnet_group_name    = aws_elasticache_subnet_group.cache_subnets.name
  security_group_ids   = [aws_security_group.elasti_cache_sg.id]
  tags = {
    Name = "my-redis-cache"
  }
}

resource "aws_elasticache_subnet_group" "cache_subnets" {
  name       = "cache-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.main.id]
  tags = {
    Name = "cache-subnet-group"
  }
}
```

---

This configuration can be deployed with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`. It assumes that the application will be configured to connect to the ElastiCache cluster instead of the database directly.

