**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up a custom Time to Live (TTL) attribute for data expiration in Amazon DynamoDB. It creates a DynamoDB table with a global secondary index (GSI) that includes a TTL attribute. The TTL attribute is configured to automatically expire items after a specified period (e.g., 1 hour). The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a DynamoDB table, and a GSI with the TTL attribute. The TTL is set using the `time_to_live_specification` block, and the table is created in the `us-west-2` region.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name           = "example-ttl-table"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "id"
  read_capacity  = 5
  write_capacity = 5

  attribute {
    name  = "id"
    type  = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name  = "ttl_attribute"
    type  = "N"
  }

  time_to_live_specification {
    enabled = true
    attribute_name = "ttl_attribute"
  }

  global_secondary_index {
    name               = "gsi-ttl-index"
    hash_key           = "id"
    range_key          = "ttl_attribute"
    projection_type    = "ALL"
    read_capacity_units = 5
    write_capacity_units = 5
  }
}
```

This configuration will create a DynamoDB table with a TTL attribute that automatically expires items after the specified time, and a GSI to support querying based on the TTL attribute.

