**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a DynamoDB table with server-side encryption enabled. The table will be configured with a primary key and will use AWS KMS (Key Management Service) to encrypt the data at rest. The KMS key will be created as part of the configuration, and the DynamoDB table will be set up to use it for encryption. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a KMS key resource, and a DynamoDB table resource with encryption enabled.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_kms_key" "dynamodb_encryption_key" {
  description             = "KMS key for DynamoDB encryption"
  deletion_window_in_days = 7
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dynamodb.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = [
          "kms:Encrypt",
          "kms:Decrypt",
          "kms:ReEncrypt*",
          "kms:GenerateDataKey*",
          "kms:DescribeKey"
        ]
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          AWS = "arn:aws:iam::${aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root"
        }
        Action = [
          "kms:CreateGrant",
          "kms:ListGrants",
          "kms:RevokeGrant"
        ]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "encrypted_table" {
  name           = "encrypted-dynamodb-table"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "id"
  read_capacity  = 5
  write_capacity = 5

  attribute {
    name = "id"
    type = "S"
  }

  server_side_encryption {
    enabled = true
    kms_key_arn = aws_kms_key.dynamodb_encryption_key.arn
  }
}
```

---

This configuration is ready to be applied with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`. It ensures that the DynamoDB table is encrypted using a KMS key, and all necessary resources are declared and configured.

