**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up the infrastructure for a video streaming site that distributes video content globally. It uses the following AWS services:

- **AWS S3**: To store the video content.
- **AWS CloudFront**: To create a global content delivery network (CDN) for fast and secure delivery of video content.
- **AWS Route53**: To manage DNS and route traffic to the CloudFront distribution.
- **AWS IAM**: To create necessary IAM roles and policies for secure access to AWS resources.

The configuration includes:
- An S3 bucket for video storage.
- A CloudFront distribution that points to the S3 bucket.
- A Route53 hosted zone and an A record that points to the CloudFront distribution.
- IAM roles and policies for secure access to S3 and CloudFront.

---

**Terraform HCL Code:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name for the video streaming site"
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "bucket_name" {
  description = "Name of the S3 bucket to store video content"
  default     = "video-streaming-bucket"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_bucket" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  server_side_encryption_configuration {
    rule {
      apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
        sse_algorithm = "AES256"
      }
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "video-streaming-bucket"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.bucket

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action = [
          "s3:GetObject"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:s3:::${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.bucket}/*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_distribution" {
  origin {
    domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name
    origin_id   = "S3-${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.bucket}"

    s3_origin_config {
      origin_access_identity = aws_cloudfront_origin_access_identity.video_oai.id
    }
  }

  enabled             = true
  is_ipv6_enabled     = true
  comment             = "CloudFront distribution for video streaming site"
  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods  = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "S3-${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.bucket}"
    forward_headers  = "all"
    viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https"
    min_ttl          = 0
    default_ttl      = 3600
    max_ttl          = 86400
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    acm_certificate_arn = aws_acm_certificate.video_cert.arn
    ssl_support_method  = "sni-only"
    minimum_protocol_version = "TLSv1.2_2021"
  }

  aliases = [var.domain_name]

  tags = {
    Name = "video-streaming-distribution"
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_origin_access_identity" "video_oai" {
  comment = "OAI for S3 bucket access"
}

resource "aws_acm_certificate" "video_cert" {
  domain_name       = var.domain_name
  validation_method = "DNS"

  tags = {
    Name = "video-streaming-certificate"
  }
}

resource "aws_acm_certificate_validation" "video_cert_validation" {
  certificate_arn         = aws_acm_certificate.video_cert.arn
  validation_record_fqdns = [aws_route53_record.video_cert_validation.fqdn]
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "video_cert_validation" {
  name      = aws_acm_certificate_validation.video_cert_validation.fqdn
  type      = "CNAME"
  zone_id   = aws_route53_zone.video_zone.id
  records   = [aws_acm_certificate_validation.video_cert_validation.cname]
  ttl       = 60
  overwrite = true
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "video_zone" {
  name = var.domain_name
  tags = {
    Name = "video-streaming-zone"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "video_distribution_alias" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.video_zone.id
  name    = var.domain_name
  type    = "A"
  alias {
    name                   = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_distribution.domain_name
    zone_id                = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_distribution.hosted_zone_id
    evaluate_target_health = false
  }
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- This configuration assumes you have already registered the domain (`example.com`) with Route53 or that you are using a domain that you can manage with Route53.
- The ACM certificate will be validated via DNS, and the Route53 record is created automatically.
- The S3 bucket is configured with versioning and server-side encryption for security and data integrity.
- The CloudFront distribution is configured to use the S3 bucket as the origin and is set up to use HTTPS with a valid certificate.

Let me know if you'd like to add video transcoding, user authentication, or other features.

