**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS Lightsail instance and grants it access to an S3 bucket. The Lightsail instance will be configured with a public IP and a basic setup. An IAM role will be created for the Lightsail instance, and the role will be granted permissions to access the specified S3 bucket. The S3 bucket will be created with public read access to allow the Lightsail instance to interact with it.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example_bucket" {
  bucket = "example-bucket-terraform"
  acl    = "public-read"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "lightsail_role" {
  name = "lightsail-s3-access-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = {
        Service = "lightsail.amazonaws.com"
      }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "s3_access" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.lightsail_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "example_instance" {
  name              = "example-lightsail-instance"
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  blueprint_id      = "ubuntu_lts"
  bundle_id         = "nano_1_0"
  user_data         = <<-EOF
    #!/bin/bash
    apt update
    apt install -y awscli
    aws s3 ls s3://${aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.bucket}
    EOF
  ssh_key_name      = "example-ssh-key"
  tags = {
    Name = "example-lightsail-instance"
  }

  iam_instance_profile {
    name = aws_iam_role.lightsail_role.name
  }
}

resource "aws_lightsail_static_ip" "example_static_ip" {
  name = "example-static-ip"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance_static_ip_attachment" "example_attachment" {
  instance_name = aws_lightsail_instance.example_instance.name
  static_ip_name  = aws_lightsail_static_ip.example_static_ip.name
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- The `aws_s3_bucket` is created with public read access to allow the Lightsail instance to access it.
- The `aws_iam_role` is created with a trust policy that allows AWS Lightsail to assume the role.
- The `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` grants the role the ability to read from S3.
- The `aws_lightsail_instance` is configured with a basic Ubuntu blueprint and a user data script that installs AWS CLI and lists the contents of the S3 bucket.
- A static IP is assigned to the Lightsail instance for consistent access.

Make sure to replace `"example-ssh-key"` with the name of an existing SSH key pair in your AWS account.

