**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration will create an AWS Lightsail Distribution with a Lightsail instance as the origin. The configuration includes:

- A Lightsail instance (origin server).
- A Lightsail distribution (CDN) that points to the instance.
- A provider configuration for AWS with a specified region.
- Default values for variables such as instance name, distribution name, and region.

This setup allows you to serve content through a CDN using a Lightsail instance as the backend.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "lightsail_instance_name" {
  description = "Name of the Lightsail instance to be used as the origin."
  default     = "my-lightsail-instance"
}

variable "lightsail_distribution_name" {
  description = "Name of the Lightsail distribution (CDN)."
  default     = "my-lightsail-distribution"
}

variable "region" {
  description = "AWS region to deploy resources."
  default     = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "origin" {
  name              = var.lightsail_instance_name
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  blueprint_id      = "app_wordpress_4_4"
  bundle_id         = "nano_1_0"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "cdn" {
  name = var.lightsail_distribution_name

  origin {
    name = aws_lightsail_instance.origin.name
    protocol_policy = "http-only"
    region_name = var.region
  }

  cache_behavior {
    path_pattern = "/*"
    behavior = "cache"
  }

  is_enabled = true
}
```

---

This configuration is ready to be applied with `terraform apply` and assumes you have the correct AWS credentials configured. It will deploy a basic WordPress instance and a CDN distribution pointing to it.

