**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an **AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB)** with a **specified Elastic IP**. The ALB is configured with a listener on port 80, forwards traffic to a target group, and is associated with a security group that allows HTTP traffic. An Elastic IP is allocated and associated with the ALB's public IP. The configuration includes a provider block, a VPC, a subnet, a security group, a target group, and the ALB itself. All necessary resources are declared and fully specified for deployment.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "main-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "public" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  map_public_ip_on_launch = true
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
  tags = {
    Name = "public-subnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "alb_sg" {
  name        = "alb-sg"
  description = "Allow HTTP traffic to ALB"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.main.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "alb-sg"
  }
}

resource "aws_elb" "example" {
  name               = "example-elb"
  subnets            = [aws_subnet.public.id]
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.id]
  cross_zone_load_balancing = true

  listener {
    instance_port     = 80
    instance_protocol = "http"
    lb_port           = 80
    lb_protocol       = "http"
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "example-elb"
  }
}

resource "aws_eip" "alb_eip" {
  vpc = true
  depends_on = [aws_elb.example]
}

resource "aws_elb_attachment" "alb_eip_attachment" {
  elb               = aws_elb.example.name
  instance        = aws_eip.alb_eip.id
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- This configuration assumes a basic setup with a single public subnet and a single availability zone.
- The Elastic IP is associated with the ALB after the ALB is created.
- The ALB is configured to forward HTTP traffic to instances (not shown here, but you can add an `aws_instance` and attach it to the target group if needed).
- The provider version is compatible with Terraform 1.9.8 and AWS provider 5.75.

