LLM Output #0:
**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) with a lifecycle policy that automatically transitions files to the Infrequent Access (IA) storage class after a specified number of days. The lifecycle policy helps reduce storage costs by moving infrequently accessed data to a lower-cost storage class. The configuration includes an EFS file system, a mount target, and an IAM role with the necessary permissions to manage the lifecycle policy.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "efs_lifecycle_role" {
  name = "efs-lifecycle-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "elasticfilesystem.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "efs_lifecycle_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.efs_lifecycle_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonEFSRoleForLifecyclePolicies"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "example" {
  creation_token = "example-efs"
  lifecycle_policies {
    transition_to_ia = "7"
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_mount_target" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id
  subnet_id      = "subnet-12345678" # Replace with a valid subnet ID
  security_groups = ["sg-12345678"] # Replace with a valid security group ID
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- Replace `"subnet-12345678"` and `"sg-12345678"` with valid subnet and security group IDs from your AWS environment.
- The `transition_to_ia` parameter in the lifecycle policy specifies the number of days after which files are moved to the Infrequent Access storage class.
- The IAM role `efs-lifecycle-role` is assumed by EFS to apply the lifecycle policy.

This configuration is compatible with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and AWS provider version `~> 5.75`.

