**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) and attaches a system-managed policy to it. The EFS is created in the `us-east-1` region, and the system policy allows the EFS to communicate with other AWS services such as Amazon EC2 and Amazon VPC. The configuration includes a default VPC and subnet selection, and it ensures that the EFS is properly secured with a system policy.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "example" {
  creation_token = "example-efs"
  tags = {
    Name = "example-efs"
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system_policy" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action = [
          "elasticfilesystem:ClientMount",
          "elasticfilesystem:ClientWrite",
          "elasticfilesystem:ClientRootAccess"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:elasticfilesystem:${aws_efs_file_system.example.region}:${aws_efs_file_system.example.owner_id}:file-system/${aws_efs_file_system.example.id}"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = [
          "elasticfilesystem:MountFileSystem"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:elasticfilesystem:${aws_efs_file_system.example.region}:${aws_efs_file_system.example.owner_id}:file-system/${aws_efs_file_system.example.id}"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

---

This configuration will create an EFS file system and apply a system policy that allows EC2 instances and other AWS services to interact with the EFS. You can modify the policy as needed to fit your specific security requirements.

